-- title:
--   Localisations of the Gauss reduction of the X₁(Mp) charts are DVRs
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 5$ an integer with $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image in $L((q))$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\mathbb{Q}$ $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A\to L$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the }j\text{-numerator power series over }\mathbb{Q})$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra. For $S\subseteq K$ the integral closure of $A[j]$ (resp. of $A[j^{-1}]$) in $K$, consider the set of $r\in k((q))$ for which there are $b\in S$ and $x,y\in A[[q]]$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction over the residue field of $A$, with $b\cdot y=x$ in $L((q))$, and $r=\bar x/\bar y$ in $k((q))$. The assertion is that for the $k$-subalgebra of $k((q))$ generated by this set, in both cases, the localisation at every maximal ideal is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   The two $k$-algebras are the affine rings of the reduced multiplicative component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$, off $j=\infty$ and off $j=0$ respectively; the statement says this component is regular at every closed point. It feeds the comparison [`ModularCurve.XOneP.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1_mul) between the chart rings and the algebras generated by these Gauss reductions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isDiscreteValuationRing_localization_atPrime_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1_mul.lean

